It's important to do something for your Valentine, whatever that may be. For us, it was ice cream this year. 

This flavour combo is absolutely amazing, the Ruby Chocolate ice cream base is decadant and the Chambord just brings it forward a little more. The Fudge pieces are amazing when you get one and the strawberry swirl is out of this world, the chambord again just helping with the intensity. 

We like this flavour so much, it's going to become a regular for our house and we hope you feel the same. 

Ingredients

Fudge:
400ml Condensed Milk
340g Dark Chocolate
Melt both ingredients and pour in to a mould. Keep in the fridge until ready. We grated ours so kept a piece in the freezer to help with grating. 

Strawberry Swirl:
100-150g Seedless Strawberry jam
1 Tbsp Chambord
Sieve the jam and add the Chambord. Keep in the fridge until ready to use

Ice Cream Base:
250ml Milk
500ml Double (Heavy Cream)
140g Sugar
110g Ruby Chocolate
2-3Tbsp Skimmed Milk Powder
1Tbsp Chambord

Combine the milk, sugar and chocolate in a pan gentyl heat to just steaming. Remove from the heat and cover in the fridge for mimimum of 4 hours. When ready to churn, add the skimmed milk powder and leave for 20 minutes. Then finally give it a really good whisk, add the cream and Chambord and churn away. 

Ours took 20-25 minutes in the ICE100 Cuisinart machine. 

